Tier F is anything ahead of NoNgNi but less than a millillion.

Tier G

basically all the numbers after tier F, Milli suffix
The first suffix is Mi. The arrangement of Mi has a difference. When putting it like MiSxVtQa, it's 1e4281.
However, when putting it like OcMi, it's 1e24003. Anything before tier G are classified as multiplicatives.
This rule also applies to the other large numbers we come across.
Extra layers and stuff:
Ce, Du, Tr, Qa, Qi, Se, Si, Ot, Ni
Mi, Mc, Na, Pi, Fm, At, Zp, Yc, Xo, Ve, Me
Due, Tre, Te, Pt, He, Hp, Oct, Ex, Ic, Mei
Dui, Tri, Teti, Pti, Hei, Hp, Oci, Eni, Tra, TeC
MTc, DTc, TrTc, TeTc, PeTc, HTc, HpT, OcT, EnT, TetC, MTetc
